[h1]ElderGPT Spirit Ring 0.10.0 — AFNM 0.7.17[/h1]
[i]A read-only, context-aware AI advisor inside Ascend From Nine Mountains.[/i]

Bring your own OpenAI-compatible or Anthropic model and ask for advice without leaving the game. ElderGPT reads the current run through the official ModAPI, builds a focused context snapshot, and adds relevant game-mechanics guidance to each conversation.

[h2]What's new in 0.10.0[/h2]
[list]
[*]Updated for AFNM 0.7.17, with the combat-result shortcut checked against the current game interface.
[*]Refreshes guidance for unified health, Charisma-based party capacity, reworked tournaments, and all nine crafting harmonies, including Captivating Cadence and Returning Cycle.
[*]Understands the new Qi and Stability cost reduction/penalty stats instead of the old cost multipliers.
[*]Adds a compact sect summary: rank, carried vault slips, accepted missions, and active or ready favour services.
[*]Tracks the focused quest and resolves translated event-history text correctly when the game language changes.
[/list]

[h2]Highlights[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Read-only by design[/b] — observes your run but does not automate combat, spend resources, or make choices.
[*][b]Live game context[/b] — equipped item stats, inventory names/counts, techniques, crafting, research, delves, quests, relationships, and sect activity. It cannot inspect unequipped item stats or hidden enemy details.
[*][b]Persistent sessions[/b] — chats are saved locally; start a new session or resume an earlier one.
[*][b]Streaming and context management[/b] — streams replies and compacts long conversations to stay within model limits.
[*][b]Optional proactive hints[/b] — suggestions after moments such as combat, travel, crafting, and time skips.
[*][b]Flexible providers[/b] — supports OpenAI-compatible endpoints, Anthropic endpoints, and compatible local servers.
[*][b]Customizable overlay[/b] — choose a persona, adjust text and panel size, and drag the panel where you want it.
[/list]

[h2]What you can ask[/h2]
[quote]"What should I focus on next?"

"How should I approach this fight?"

"Compare my equipped armor."

"What is holding back this craft?"

"Explain how my selected harmony changes the targets."

"Which quests or resources should I prioritize?"[/quote]

[h2]Quick start[/h2]
[list]
[*]Open the floating [b]Spirit Ring[/b] button.
[*]Open [b]Settings[/b] and choose OpenAI Compatible or Anthropic.
[*]Enter the endpoint URL, API key if required, and exact model ID.
[*]Choose Elder, Calculator, or a custom persona, then start chatting.
[/list]

[h2]Provider setup[/h2]
The mod does not bundle a model or API key. Use a provider you already trust, an aggregator such as [url=https://openrouter.ai/docs/quickstart]OpenRouter[/url], or a local OpenAI-compatible server such as [url=https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp]llama.cpp[/url] or [url=https://github.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp]KoboldCpp[/url].

Provider plans, models, and limits change often, so check your provider's current documentation. Faster models generally feel better for in-game use. ElderGPT detects context/output limits from supported APIs when possible, and manual overrides are available in Settings.

[h2]Privacy and data[/h2]
[list]
[*]Your endpoint settings, API key, UI preferences, and chat sessions are stored in the game's local browser storage.
[*]When you send a message, the mod sends the conversation and a focused snapshot of relevant game state to your configured endpoint.
[*]If you enable proactive hints, they also send automatic requests with current game context to that endpoint.
[*]Nothing is sent to a service operated by this mod's author.
[*]Use only an endpoint you trust and a key you can revoke.
[/list]

[h2]Feedback and source[/h2]
If advice is wrong or a feature misbehaves, include what you were doing in-game and what the advisor said.
[url=https://github.com/lemon07r/ElderGPT-Spirit-Ring/issues]Report an issue on GitHub[/url] or leave a Workshop comment.

